<!-- HERO -->
<section class="lib-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="lib-wrap">
    <div class="lib-hero-product" id="hero-title">mcp-librarian</div>
    <div class="lib-hero-badge">v{{ versions.librarian.version }}</div>
    <p class="lib-hero-tagline">A local, signed skill library for your AI agent</p>
    <p class="lib-hero-desc">An MCP server that keeps a folder of Markdown skills on disk, searches them with BM25, and serves the matching sections to your agent. Each skill is Ed25519-signed on write and checked on load &mdash; if a file changed since signing, the server reports <code>TAMPERED</code> rather than serving it. No config files, no dependencies beyond Node.js built-ins. Apache-2.0. Works with Claude Code, Cursor, Windsurf, local models via Ollama/LM Studio, and other MCP clients.</p>
    <p class="lib-hero-desc">Experimental and pre-1.0. It works, but it is early and lightly tested outside my own use. Expect rough edges, and please report what breaks.</p>
    <div class="lib-hero-actions">
      <a href="https://github.com/penumbraforge/mcp-librarian" class="lib-btn lib-btn-outline" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">View on GitHub</a>
